              justifications: [{ claim: "D is measured only by A, B, C", ref: "IX.13" }] },
            { text: "And, by hypothesis, {P} is not the same with any of the numbers {A}, {B}, or {C},",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["P","A","B","C"] },
            { text: "therefore {P} does not measure {D}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["P","D"] },
            { text: "But {P} is to {D} as {E} is to {Q}, therefore neither does {E} measure {Q}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["P","D","E","Q"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "E does not measure Q", ref: "VII.Def.20" }] },
            { text: "And {E} is prime, and any prime number is prime to any number which it does not measure.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E"] },
            { text: "Therefore {E} and {Q} are relatively prime.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","Q"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "E and Q are relatively prime", ref: "VII.29" }] },
            { text: "But primes are also least,",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","Q"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "primes are least", ref: "VII.21" }] },
            { text: "and the least numbers measure those which have the same ratio the same number of times,",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","Q","P","D"] },
            { text: "the antecedent the antecedent and the consequent the consequent,",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","Q","P","D"] },
            { text: "and {E} is to {Q} as {P} is to {D},",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","Q","P","D"] },
            { text: "therefore {E} measures {P} the same number of times that {Q} measures {D}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","P","Q","D"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "least numbers measure those in the same ratio", ref: "VII.20" }] },
            { text: "But {D} is not measured by any other number except {A}, {B}, or {C},",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["D","A","B","C"] },
            { text: "therefore {Q} is the same with one of the numbers {A}, {B}, or {C}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["Q","A","B","C"] },
            { text: "Let it be the same with {B}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["Q","B"] },
            { text: "And, however many {B}, {C}, and {D} are in multitude,",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["B","C","D"] },
            { text: "take so many {E}, {HK}, and {L} beginning from {E}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","HK","L"] },
            { text: "Now {E}, {HK}, and {L} are in the same ratio with {B}, {C}, and {D},",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["E","HK","L","B","C","D"] },
            { text: "therefore, ex aequali {B} is to {D} as {E} is to {L}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["B","D","E","L"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "ex aequali B : D = E : L", ref: "VII.14" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the product of {B} and {L} equals the product of {D} and {E}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["B","L","D","E"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "B × L = D × E", ref: "VII.19" }] },
            { text: "But the product of {D} and {E} equals the product of {Q} and {P},",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["D","E","Q","P"] },
            { text: "therefore the product of {Q} and {P} also equals the product of {B} and {L}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["Q","P","B","L"] },
            { text: "Therefore {Q} is to {B} as {L} is to {P}.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["Q","B","L","P"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "Q : B = L : P", ref: "VII.19" }] },
            { text: "And {Q} is the same with {B}, therefore {L} is also the same with {P},",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["Q","B","L","P"] },
            { text: "which is impossible, for by hypothesis {P} is not the same with any of the numbers set out.",
              visible: WITHQ,
              highlighted: ["P"] },
            { text: "Therefore no number measures {FG} except {A}, {B}, {C}, {D}, {E}, {HK}, {L}, {M}, and the unit.",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["FG","A","B","C","D","E","HK","L","M"] },
            { text: "And {FG} was proved equal to the sum of {A}, {B}, {C}, {D}, {E}, {HK}, {L}, {M}, and the unit,",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["FG","A","B","C","D","E","HK","L","M"] },
            { text: "and a perfect number is that which equals its own parts,",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "perfect number", ref: "VII.Def.22" }] },
            { text: "therefore {FG} is perfect.",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["FG"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit are set out continuously in double proportion",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["A","B","C","D"] },
            { text: "until the sum of all becomes prime,",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["E"] },
            { text: "and if the sum multiplied into the last makes some number,",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["E","D","FG"] },
            { text: "then the product is perfect.",
              visible: WITHNO,
              highlighted: ["FG"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "IX.36") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "VII.Def.20": "/elements/books/bookVII/definitions/defVII20/",
        "VII.Def.22": "/elements/books/bookVII/definitions/defVII22/",
